  {
   "id": "hwpf",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4: hardware prefetching. The hardware guesses which blocks come next, and fetches them before they are asked for."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 4 of 8: hardware prefetching"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "co"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "hp"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The simplest: on a miss to block i, also fetch block i plus 1. It suits code, and arrays read in order."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hp[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A stream buffer holds the next few blocks beside the cache, so wrong guesses do not evict anything."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hp[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A stride prefetcher notices a load stepping by a fixed distance, say every 256 bytes, and runs ahead along it. Modern cores, the Core i7 among them, prefetch into L1 and L2."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hp[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Why it helps, in a timeline. Each loop iteration computes for 30 cycles, and needs a new block that takes 30 cycles to fetch."
     },
     "do": [
