  {
   "id": "hbm",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 6: HBM as an extra cache level. Put a gigabyte of stacked DRAM in the package, and use it as an L4 cache in front of main memory."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 6 of 8: HBM as an extra cache level"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "cpm"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "hb"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The problem is the tags. With 64 byte blocks, 1 gigabyte is 2 to the 24 blocks. At 6 bytes of tag and state each, that is 96 megabytes of tags: far more SRAM than the chip has."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hb[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Use 4 kilobyte blocks, and the tags shrink to 1.5 megabytes. But every miss moves 4 kilobytes, most of it never used."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hb[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Or keep 64 byte blocks, and store the tags in the HBM itself. Now each access needs two DRAM reads: first the tag, then the data."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hb[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The alloy cache fixes that: direct-mapped, with each tag stored right beside its data, so one burst brings both. One access, not two."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "hb[3]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Designs also add a predictor that guesses a miss early, and starts the main memory access at once."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "hb[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "an HBM cache lives or dies by where its tags are kept"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
